00:04:09,599 --> 00:04:15,599
In the future, the odds of survival are 1000 to 1.
That's just the way she likes it.

2
00:08:19,199 --> 00:08:25,199
Tank Girl is a action, comedy, science fiction film directed by Rachel Talalay.

3
00:12:28,799 --> 00:12:34,799
After a comet disrupts the rain cycle of Earth, the planet has
become a desolate, barren desert by the year 2033.

4
00:16:38,399 --> 00:16:44,399
With resources scarce, Kesslee, head of the powerful and evil Water & Power
Corporation, the de facto government, has taken control of the water supply.

5
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:54,000
Unwilling to cower under Kesslee's tyrannical rule, a pair of outlaws known as Tank Girl and Jet
Girl rise up, joining the mysterious rebel Rippers to destroy the corrupt system.

6
00:24:57,599 --> 00:25:03,599
Rebecca / Tank Girl, played by Lori Petty.

7
00:29:07,200 --> 00:29:13,200
Jet Girl, played by Naomi Watts.

8
00:33:16,799 --> 00:33:22,799
Kesslee, played by Malcolm McDowell.

9
00:37:26,400 --> 00:37:32,400
T-Saint, played by Ice-T.

10
00:41:36,000 --> 00:41:42,000
Booga, played by Jeff Kober.

11
00:45:45,599 --> 00:45:51,599
Deetee, played by Reg E. Cathey.

12
00:49:55,199 --> 00:50:01,199
Tank Girl is a 1995 American post-apocalyptic science fiction film
directed by Rachel Talalay and written by Tedi Sarafian.

13
00:54:04,799 --> 00:54:10,799
Based on the British comics series created by Jamie Hewlett and Alan Martin, the
film stars Lori Petty, Naomi Watts, Ice-T, and Malcolm McDowell.

14
00:58:14,400 --> 00:58:20,400
Set in a drought ravaged Australia years after a catastrophic impact event, it follows the antihero Tank Girl (Petty) as she, Jet Girl (Watts),
and genetically modified supersoldiers called the Rippers fight Water & Power, an oppressive corporation led by Kesslee (McDowell).

15
01:02:24,000 --> 01:02:30,000
After reading an issue of the Tank Girl comic she had received as a gift, Talalay obtained
permission from the comic's publisher Deadline to direct a film adaptation.

16
01:06:33,599 --> 01:06:39,599
She selected Catherine Hardwicke to be the production designer, and worked
closely with Martin and Hewlett during the making of the film.

17
01:10:43,199 --> 01:10:49,199
Tank Girl was filmed primarily in White Sands, New Mexico, and Tucson, Arizona.

18
01:14:52,800 --> 01:14:58,800
The film's critically praised soundtrack was assembled by Courtney Love, and the
Rippers' makeup and prosthetics team was headed by Stan Winston.

19
01:19:02,399 --> 01:19:08,399
Winston's studio were so enthusiastic about the project they cut
their usual prices in half to meet the film's budget.

20
01:23:12,000 --> 01:23:18,000
Financially unsuccessful, Tank Girl recouped only about $6 million of its $25
million budget at the box office and received mixed reviews from critics.

21
01:27:21,599 --> 01:27:27,599
Martin and Hewlett have since spoken negatively of their experiences creating the film, and Talalay
blamed some of the film's negative reception on studio edits over which she had no control.

22
01:31:31,199 --> 01:31:37,199
Despite the box-office failure of the film, it has since become a cult
classic and has been noted for its feminist themes.

23
01:35:40,800 --> 01:35:46,800
The film explores themes of dystopia, destroy,
reincarnation, based on comic, desert.

24
01:39:50,399 --> 01:39:56,399
The tone is lighthearted and thought_provoking.
